-- title:
--   Nine integrality relations for a prime Hecke idele at q
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q'$ be a prime such that $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$, every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit exactly when $q'$ lies in $v$; that is, $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $q'$. Let $\Lambda_1\subset\mathbb{H}$ be a maximal order (an order, in the sense of containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning $\mathbb{H}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and finitely generated, maximal among such), write $\widehat{\Lambda}_1=$ [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$ for the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}^f_{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adele, and for a unit $g$ write $\Lambda_1^g=$ [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) $\Lambda_1\,g$ for the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ of elements whose image under $\mathrm{includeLeft}$ lies in $g\,\widehat{\Lambda}_1\,g^{-1}$. Let $N\geq 1$, and let $m$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}^f_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $m\in\widehat{\Lambda}_1$ and $N\,m^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda}_1$, such that $\Lambda_1^m$ is a maximal order, and let $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_1^m$ have index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$ (relative index of the underlying additive subgroups). Let $q$ be a prime with $q\nmid N$ and $q'\nmid Nq$. Let $m'$ be a unit with $m'\in\widehat{\Lambda}_1$ and $Nq\,m'^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda}_1$, with $\Lambda_1^{m'}$ a maximal order, and let $S=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_1^{m'}$ have index $Nq$ in $\Lambda_1$. Finally let $n$ be a unit belonging to the prime Hecke set of $R$ at $q$, i.e. $n\in\widehat{R}$, $q\,n^{-1}\in\widehat{R}$, $n^{-1}\notin\widehat{R}$ and $q^{-1}n\notin\widehat{R}$, and assume $S=R\cap R^{n}$ and $S^{n}=S$. Then the nine elements $n$, $q\,n^{-1}$, $n^{-1}m'$, $N\,m'^{-1}n$, $q^{-1}nm'$, $q\,(nn)^{-1}$, $q^{-1}nn$, $m'^{-1}nm'$ and $q\,m'^{-1}n^{-1}m'$ all lie in $\widehat{\Lambda}_1$.
--
--   The statement records the idelic integrality properties of an element realising, at the raised prime $q$, the passage from the Eichler order $R$ of index $N$ in the maximal order $\Lambda_1$ to the Eichler order $S$ of index $Nq$, together with the relations between such an element $n$ and the idele $m'$ cutting out $S$; they are the form in which Atkin–Lehner type normalisers of $S$ at $q$ enter the combinatorics of the Čerednik–Drinfeld class-set graph. It feeds the analysis of kernel ideals and dual pairs for the class set at level $Nq$ in [`CerednikDrinfeld.image_kernelIdealSet_comp_eq_star_smul_ofFiniteIdele_mul_and_exists_dualPair_ker_eq_map_of_meetOrder_eq_of_conjByFiniteIdele_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.image_kernelIdealSet_comp_eq_star_smul_ofFiniteIdele_mul_and_exists_dualPair_ker_eq_map_of_meetOrder_eq_of_conjByFiniteIdele_eq).
